From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Linux app windows open at their size

Exo creates a shell surface's widget at the client's first commit, with
an empty placeholder for bounds (1x1) until its first frame. GTK 4 asks
for state changes in between, unsetting maximized and fullscreen on every
new window, and each is answered with a configure carrying the widget's
bounds: the client sizes itself to 1x1, so every GTK 4 window opened at
its minimum size (a 480x320 GtkGLArea window at 157x66) on the Dell and
in the VM. Crostini's apps go through sommelier; NickelOS's talk to Exo
directly. Until the window is first shown, such a configure now carries
an empty size (the client chooses), as the one sent before the widget
existed does; bounds the window has been given (window restore, 0018)
still go out.

diff --git a/components/exo/shell_surface.cc b/components/exo/shell_surface.cc
index bd75e835f5ad6..79e9e38d06d1e 100644
--- a/components/exo/shell_surface.cc
+++ b/components/exo/shell_surface.cc
@@ -1043,9 +1043,23 @@ void ShellSurface::Configure(bool ends_drag) {
       auto occlusion_state = occlusion_observer_->state();
       auto restore_state_type = std::optional<chromeos::WindowStateType>{
           window_state->GetRestoreWindowState()};
+      // NickelOS: the widget exists from the client's first commit, but its
+      // bounds are an empty placeholder, 1x1, until its first frame. Linux
+      // apps talk to Exo directly (Crostini's go through sommelier), and GTK
+      // 4 asks for state changes then (unset maximized and fullscreen on
+      // every new window), each answered with a configure: sizing the client
+      // to 1x1 opened every GTK 4 window at its minimum size. Until the
+      // window is first shown, an empty size (0x0: the client chooses) goes
+      // out instead, as in the configure sent before the widget existed.
+      // Bounds it has been given (window restore) still do.
+      gfx::Rect bounds = GetClientBoundsInScreen(widget_);
+      if (!widget_->IsVisible() && !widget_->IsMinimized() &&
+          bounds.width() <= 1 && bounds.height() <= 1) {
+        bounds.set_size(gfx::Size());
+      }
       serial = configure_callback_.Run(
-          GetClientBoundsInScreen(widget_), window_state->GetStateType(),
-          IsResizing(), widget_->IsActive(), origin_offset,
+          bounds, window_state->GetStateType(), IsResizing(),
+          widget_->IsActive(), origin_offset,
           /*raster_scale=*/1.0, occlusion_state, restore_state_type);
     } else {
       auto state = chromeos::ToWindowStateType(initial_show_state_);
